11
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
The Addams Family is a 1991 American supernatural black comedy film based
on the comic strip characters created by Charles Addams.

12
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:38,727
Directed by former cinematographer Barry Sonnenfeld in his feature directorial debut, the film stars Anjelica Huston, who was nominated for
a Golden Globe for her performance as Morticia Addams, Raul Julia as Gomez Addams, and Christopher Lloyd as Fester Addams.

13
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:11,454
The film focuses on a bizarre, macabre, aristocratic family who reconnect with someone
whom they believe to be a long-lost relative, Gomez's brother Fester Addams.

14
01:03:38,181 --> 01:03:44,181
The film was noted for its turbulent production.

15
01:08:10,909 --> 01:08:16,909
Originally developed at Orion Pictures, the film went $5 million over budget due to constant rewrites throughout shooting; health problems
of people involved in the filming; and an overall stressful filming for Sonnenfeld himself, which caused multiple delays.

16
01:12:43,636 --> 01:12:49,636
The rise in production costs from the film's $25 million budget to $30 million led Orion, financially struggling and fearful of another
big-budget flop, to sell the film to Paramount Pictures, who completed the film and handled the film's domestic distribution.

17
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
Orion distributed the film internationally through Columbia Tri-Star Films.

18
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film was commercially successful, making back
almost seven times its production costs.

19
01:26:21,818 --> 01:26:27,818
A sequel, Addams Family Values, was released in 1993.

20
01:30:54,545 --> 01:31:00,545
The film explores themes of dancing, dead wish,
secret passage, fencing, black humor.

21
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
The tone is lighthearted.
